# Cloudflare Pages cache rules.
#
# Every path revalidates by default, and only the media directories are allowed
# a long cache. "no-cache" does not mean "do not cache": the browser keeps its
# copy and asks with an ETag, so an unchanged file costs a 304 and a changed one
# is picked up at once.
#
# The default is /* rather than /*.html because Pages serves extensionless URLs:
# the page people actually visit is /events, and a /*.html rule never matches it.
# Later rules override earlier ones, so the media overrides below still win.
#
# This exists because a stale js/events.js was left running against fresh HTML
# after an element it referenced was deleted. It threw, and took the whole
# events calendar down with it while the page looked fine above the fold.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Media is content-addressed by name in practice: a changed photograph or clip
# gets a new filename. Long cache, and it never goes stale in a way that breaks.
/assets/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000

/assets/video/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000

/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
